**Definition 10.2 (the unresolved minimization obligation).** For unequal allowed sources in $0<2\epsilon<\kappa$, define

$$
L=6+\min(N_1,J+1),\qquad
V=\min(6+N_1,7+K_{\mathrm{geo}}).
$$

Theorems 4.3 and 6.1 give $L\le N_{\mathrm{gen}}\le V$. Theorem 6.3 decides whether the first candidate $7+N_2$ is attainable when $N_1\ge N_2+2$, and Corollary 6.4 raises the lower integer if it is not. The still-open obligation is to determine the minimum in every remaining unmatched regime, under the entire competitor class of Definition 1.3.

In particular, a proof must account for additional transient configurations, periodic $B$ tails with several phases, duplicated exact recurrent source presentations, exits through synchronized transient configurations, arbitrary emission proportions and holding probabilities, and configurations reached only on generated words. Recurrent exactness alone does not reduce those presentations to the fixed-holding family. The first-candidate counting proof does not apply when additional labels remain. A matching unrestricted invariant or a further counted all-history, all-horizon construction is required. Analytical elimination of the general-holding feasibility criterion for all real parameters is also not supplied. The exact value of $C_{\mathrm{tail}}$ solves only its specified family optimization.

